 "title": "GTA 6 won't let you steal a supercar on day one",
 "audio": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3Lh3gaSoJDsjYAzqFyj65XamsxE/hf_20261116_053333_a6bffcbf-2648-4c85-828a-c948a202ce24.wav",
 "script": "In GTA 6, you can't steal a supercar on day one. Rockstar showed The Guardian that Jason and Lucia start out only able to hotwire cheap cars and pick basic locks. Better jobs unlock later. So instead of pulling a gun in a crowd, you scope out a target, disable cameras and find a back door. Skip the planning and it escalates fast. In the demo, a guard opened fire, then police cars and helicopters chased them. Rockstar says it won't punish players who go loud, but your actions will have some effect. Is this better, or less fun? Comment your pick.",
